85814d79-90bf-45a5-9b9e-19eba5fe6081	London: National Gallery Private Tour - Da Vinci to Van Gogh	london-national-gallery-private-tour-da-vinci-to-van-gogh-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Museum Tour	Private tour	null	draft	Experience a private tour at the National Gallery discovering how painting was used to promote religion and power from early icons to modern art.	Experience a private tour at the National Gallery. Discover how painting was used to promote religion and power across time, from early icons to Renaissance, Baroque and modern art. You will encounter works by Leonardo da Vinci, Raphael and Michelangelo, where careful observation brings new depth to the depiction of Christ. Their paintings transform how sacred figures are understood. The journey continues with Baroque art, where the use of light and realism creates powerful, immediate scenes that draw the viewer directly into the moment. It then extends into later developments, including Impressionism and modern art. Works by Van Gogh and Monet reveal new ways of seeing the world through colour and perception. Along the way, the tour considers how painting supported both religious and royal authority, shaping ideas of belief, power and identity across different periods. Selected works are used to illustrate these changes, offering a clear and focused route through the collection. Throughout the experience, the focus remains on how painting evolves: from symbolic images to lifelike presence and into later and modern interpretations of art. The tour also explores how nudity is used in art, including its role within Christian imagery. It also touches on themes inspired by classical mythology and ancient history.	["Explore the museum with an expert guide through a clear and engaging narrative", "Follow a focused journey from early icons to Renaissance, Baroque and modern art", "Discover how art expresses belief, power and human emotion", "Experience the shift from symbolic images to dramatic, lifelike scenes", "Encounter works by Leonardo da Vinci, Raphael and Michelangelo", "See works by Van Gogh and Monet revealing new ways of seeing through colour", "Learn how painting supported religious and royal authority across periods", "Explore themes of classical mythology and ancient history in art"]	["Private professional art guide", "Skip-the-line entry to National Gallery", "Personalized tour itinerary", "In-depth commentary on selected masterpieces", "Flexible duration based on your interests"]	["Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Food and beverages", "Gratuities for guide", "Special exhibition tickets (if applicable)", "Audio equipment (not needed for private tour)"]	Comfortable walking shoes, camera (photography allowed in most areas), water bottle, and any specific questions about artworks you'd like to discuss	The National Gallery is free to enter, but this private tour includes expert guidance and skip-the-line convenience. Photography is permitted in most areas but flash photography is prohibited. Some galleries may be temporarily closed for maintenance.	180.00	120.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["10:00", "14:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour start time. Cancellations within 24 hours may incur charges.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	National Gallery	Meet your guide at the main entrance of the National Gallery on Trafalgar Square, near the information desk	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739150/rayna/activities/85814d79-90bf-45a5-9b9e-19eba5fe6081/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739150/rayna/activities/85814d79-90bf-45a5-9b9e-19eba5fe6081/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: National Gallery Private Tour - Da Vinci to Van Gogh - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/85814d79-90b