198a19a7-40db-4812-b863-3033f1ab4aa7	London: Jack the Ripper Small Group Tour	london-jack-the-ripper-small-group-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Historical Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Explore the gruesome history of Jack the Ripper through the very streets where the infamous murders occurred.	Our knowledgeable guides are seasoned experts on the gruesome history of Jack the Ripper. They'll lead you through the very streets where the infamous murders occurred, offering insights and intriguing theories that will leave you on the edge of your seat. The tour is available to book in English or in Spanish, please select your preference at checkout. Why choose our tour: Unparalleled Historical Accuracy: We've meticulously researched the facts, myths, and legends surrounding Jack the Ripper to provide you with the most accurate and spine-chilling experience. Small Group Tours: Enjoy an intimate tour experience with our small group sizes, ensuring you have the opportunity to engage with our expert guides and ask questions. Interactive Experience: Our tours are immersive and interactive, with captivating stories, evidence, and re-enactments that transport you back to the eerie streets of Victorian London. Notable neighbours and landmarks: Whitechapel: Begin your journey in the heart of Whitechapel, the epicentre of the Ripper's reign of terror. Stroll along Whitechapel Road, where many of the victims met their gruesome fate. Spitalfields: Immerse yourself in the rich history of Spitalfields, a district steeped in Victorian charm. Explore the bustling Spitalfields Market and discover its hidden secrets. Ten Bells Pub: Visit the legendary Ten Bells Pub, where several of the Ripper's victims were said to have frequented. It's an eerie experience you won't soon forget. Brick Lane: Wander down Brick Lane, known for its vibrant street art and diverse culinary scene. Learn how this area has transformed over the years while staying true to its gritty past. Aldgate East: Uncover the secrets of Aldgate East, another location with ties to the Ripper. Learn about the investigations and the mysteries that still linger to this day.	["Small group intimate experience", "Expert guides with historical accuracy", "Interactive stories and re-enactments", "Visit Whitechapel and Spitalfields", "See Ten Bells Pub and Brick Lane", "Explore Aldgate East mysteries", "Optional museum entry upgrade"]	["Expert guide with extensive Jack the Ripper knowledge", "Small group walking tour", "Visit to historic murder sites", "Access to Ten Bells Pub area", "Historical facts and evidence presentation", "Interactive storytelling experience"]	["Food and drinks", "Transportation to meeting point", "Gratuities", "Personal expenses", "Hotel pickup and drop-off"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, and a camera. The tour operates in all weather conditions.	This tour contains graphic content about violent crimes and is not suitable for children under 12. The tour involves walking on uneven Victorian streets and may not be suitable for those with mobility issues.	25.00	\N	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["13:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	t	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour start time. No refund for cancellations within 24 hours.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Whitechapel Station	Meet outside Whitechapel Underground Station, Exit 1. Look for the guide with a Ripper Tours sign.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en", "es"]	https://cdn.getyourguide.com/image/format=auto,fit=crop,gravity=auto,quality=60,width=285,height=160/tour_img/4e33603f402c10f9.jpeg	\N	\N	\N	0	0	0	0	\N	Jack the Ripper Small Group Tour in London | Rayna Tours	Explore Jack the Ripper's murder sites on this chilling small group walking tour through Whitechapel. Expert guides reveal Victorian London's darkest secre	Jack the Ripper tour London	\N	\N	https://www