0aa096d0-48f4-4c67-b258-03b14f63a315	From London: Full-Day Cotswolds Villages Group Tour	from-london-full-day-cotswolds-villages-group-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Countryside Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Full-day group tour from London exploring the charming villages and countryside of the Cotswolds region.	Escape the bustling streets of London and immerse yourself in the quintessential English countryside with this full-day Cotswolds Villages Group Tour. Journey through one of England's most picturesque regions, designated as an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty, where honey-colored limestone cottages, rolling green hills, and charming market towns create a storybook landscape that has remained virtually unchanged for centuries.\n\nYour comfortable coach will wind through narrow country lanes, taking you to some of the Cotswolds' most beloved villages. Explore the medieval streets of Chipping Campden with its magnificent 15th-century church and historic market hall, or wander through Bourton-on-the-Water, often called the 'Venice of the Cotswolds' for its low bridges spanning the River Windrush. Visit the romantic village of Stow-on-the-Wold, famous for its antique shops and traditional pubs surrounding the market square.\n\nEach village offers its own unique character and charm, from thatched-roof cottages adorned with climbing roses to traditional tea rooms serving homemade scones with clotted cream. You'll have ample time to explore independently, browse local craft shops, and capture Instagram-worthy photos of the stunning architecture and countryside views.\n\nThis carefully curated tour provides the perfect introduction to the Cotswolds for first-time visitors, combining the convenience of organized transportation with the freedom to explore at your own pace. Your knowledgeable guide will share fascinating stories about the region's history, from its wool-trading heritage to its connections with famous writers and artists who found inspiration in these idyllic surroundings.\n\nReturn to London in the evening with unforgettable memories of England's most beautiful countryside, having experienced the timeless charm that makes the Cotswolds a UNESCO World Heritage candidate and one of the country's most treasured destinations.	["Visit multiple charming Cotswolds villages including Chipping Campden and Bourton-on-the-Water", "Explore honey-colored limestone cottages and traditional English countryside", "Enjoy free time to browse antique shops, craft stores, and traditional tea rooms", "Travel in comfort with round-trip transportation from central London", "Learn about the region's rich history and wool-trading heritage from your guide", "Experience the 'Venice of the Cotswolds' and picturesque market towns", "Capture stunning photos of quintessential English village scenes", "Discover an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty just outside London"]	["Round-trip transportation by comfortable coach from London", "Professional English-speaking guide", "Visits to multiple Cotswolds villages", "Free time for independent exploration in each village", "Commentary about local history and culture"]	["Food and drinks", "Entrance fees to attractions", "Personal expenses and souvenirs", "Gratuities for guide and driver", "Travel insurance"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for purchases and refreshments in the villages.	This tour involves walking on uneven surfaces and cobblestone streets. Villages may be crowded during peak tourist season. Some shops and attractions may be closed on Sundays.	65.00	45.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	600	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour departure time for a full refund.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Victoria Coach Station	Meet at Victoria Coach Station, Gate 1-5 area. Look for the tour ope