374bf84d-1223-40e7-b0a1-c56966ae9eee	London: London Eye, River Cruise, & Hop-on Hop-off Bus Tour	london-london-eye-river-cruise-hop-on-hop-off-bus-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Sightseeing	Self-guided	null	draft	Combination tour including London Eye ride, Thames river cruise, and hop-on hop-off bus tour for 1-2 days of sightseeing.	Experience the best of London with this comprehensive combination tour that includes three of the city's most popular sightseeing experiences. Begin your adventure with a ride on the iconic London Eye, where you'll enjoy breathtaking 360-degree views of the capital from 135 meters above the Thames. This 30-minute rotation offers unparalleled photo opportunities of landmarks including Big Ben, Westminster Abbey, St. Paul's Cathedral, and the Tower of London.\n\nNext, embark on a relaxing Thames River Cruise that provides a unique perspective of London's historic waterfront. Glide past the Houses of Parliament, Tower Bridge, Shakespeare's Globe Theatre, and the modern Shard skyscraper while learning about the city's rich maritime history through informative commentary.\n\nComplete your London exploration with a flexible hop-on hop-off bus tour featuring multiple routes that connect all major attractions. With buses running every 10-20 minutes, you can explore at your own pace, stopping at over 60 locations including Buckingham Palace, Trafalgar Square, Oxford Street, Camden Market, and Greenwich. The open-top double-decker buses provide excellent views and multilingual audio commentary sharing fascinating stories about London's history, culture, and architecture.\n\nThis combination package offers exceptional value and convenience, allowing you to see London from land, water, and sky. The flexible nature of the hop-on hop-off service means you can spend as much time as you like at each attraction, making it perfect for first-time visitors who want to get oriented with the city layout while experiencing its most famous landmarks.	["Optional audio guide"]	["London Eye standard admission ticket", "40-minute Thames River Cruise", "1 or 2-day hop-on hop-off bus tour", "Multilingual audio commentary on bus", "Live commentary on river cruise", "Access to multiple bus routes covering central London", "Free Wi-Fi on buses", "Route maps and attraction information"]	["Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Food and beverages", "Gratuities", "Admission to attractions (except London Eye)", "Fast-track London Eye tickets", "Personal expenses", "Travel insurance"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, sunscreen, and a valid photo ID. Consider bringing layers as weather can change throughout the day.	London Eye tickets are timed entry - please arrive at your designated time slot. Bus services may be affected by traffic and weather conditions. River cruise operates weather permitting. Some bus routes may have seasonal variations.	85.00	60.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	1440	["09:00", "10:00", "11:00", "12:00", "13:00", "14:00", "15:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the experience starts. No refund for cancellations made less than 24 hours before start time.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	London Eye Ticket Office	Meet at the London Eye ticket office located on the South Bank of the Thames, near Westminster Bridge. The nearest tube stations are Westminster and Waterloo.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738453/rayna/activities/374bf84d-1223-40e7-b0a1-c56966ae9eee/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738453/rayna/activities/374bf84d-1223-40e7-b0a1-c56966ae9eee/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: London Eye, River Cruise, & Hop-on Hop-off Bus Tour - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/374bf84d-1223-40e7-b0a1-c56966ae9eee