8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285	Bloomsbury Walking Tour: Hidden London & Georgian Shadows	bloomsbury-walking-tour-hidden-london-georgian-shadows-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Walking Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Explore Bloomsbury's Georgian squares and hidden histories, uncovering tales of royal scandal, literary legends, and Victorian philanthropists.	Step beyond the guidebooks into Bloomsbury's leafy Georgian squares, elegant townhouses, and hidden cobbled mews as you uncover the stories of the rich, the poor, the forgotten, and the Victorian philanthropists who tried to change their world. On this walking tour, hear tales of royal scandal, abandoned children, a world‑famous children's hospital, and literary legends including J. M. Barrie and Charles Dickens. Discover where George III was treated for his "madness," see the former home of Virginia Woolf, and visit the church where Ted Hughes and Sylvia Plath were married, once known as the church of the chimney sweeps. Meet an unscrupulous property developer with a very strange name and step inside a grand hotel with remarkable links to the Titanic. Every stop reveals a different layer of Bloomsbury, from Georgian elegance to hidden histories and extraordinary human stories.	["Explore Bloomsbury's leafy Georgian squares and elegant townhouses", "Discover hidden cobbled mews and forgotten stories", "Learn about literary legends including J.M. Barrie and Charles Dickens", "Visit Virginia Woolf's former home", "See the church where Ted Hughes and Sylvia Plath were married", "Hear tales of royal scandal and George III's treatment", "Visit a grand hotel with Titanic connections", "Uncover stories of Victorian philanthropists and social change"]	["Expert local guide", "Walking tour of Bloomsbury's historic sites", "Stories and historical commentary", "Access to hidden squares and mews"]	["Food and drinks", "Transportation to meeting point", "Entrance fees to attractions", "Gratuities"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, umbrella if rain is expected	This is a walking tour covering approximately 2-3 miles. The tour operates in most weather conditions, so please dress appropriately. Some stops may involve uneven surfaces or cobblestones.	25.00	18.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["10:30", "14:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Russell Square Underground Station	Meet outside the main entrance to Russell Square Underground Station, near the statue of Francis Russell	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738667/rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738667/rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/0.jpg", "alt_text": "Bloomsbury Walking Tour: Hidden London & Georgian Shadows - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738669/rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/1.jpg", "alt_text": "Bloomsbury Walking Tour: Hidden London & Georgian Shadows - image 2", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/1"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738671/rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/2.jpg", "alt_text": "Bloomsbury Walking Tour: Hidden London & Georgian Shadows - image 3", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/2"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738673/rayna/activities/8a73cdff-bed9-45fa-b76c-f4af37d42285/3.jpg", "alt_text": "Bloomsbury Walking Tour: Hidden London & Georgian 