8e443588-b27b-4e80-b27e-6553ed96dca3	From London: Stonehenge & Roman Baths Full-Day Trip	from-london-stonehenge-roman-baths-full-day-trip-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Historical Sites	Group tour	null	draft	Full-day excursion from London to explore the ancient Stonehenge monument and the historic Roman Baths in Bath.	Embark on an unforgettable full-day journey from London to discover two of England's most iconic historical treasures: the mysterious Stonehenge and the magnificent Roman Baths in Bath. This comprehensive tour combines ancient wonder with Roman sophistication, offering a perfect introduction to Britain's rich heritage.\n\nYour adventure begins with a scenic drive through the English countryside to Stonehenge, one of the world's most famous prehistoric monuments. Standing majestically on Salisbury Plain, this 5,000-year-old stone circle continues to captivate visitors with its enigmatic purpose and remarkable construction. Walk around the ancient stones while listening to fascinating theories about its origins, from astronomical calendar to sacred burial ground. The state-of-the-art visitor center provides compelling insights through interactive exhibits and a 360-degree virtual experience.\n\nContinue to the elegant Georgian city of Bath, a UNESCO World Heritage Site renowned for its stunning architecture and natural hot springs. Explore the remarkably preserved Roman Baths, where you can walk on ancient pavements and see the Sacred Spring, Roman Temple, and the Great Bath. Marvel at the engineering prowess of the Romans as you discover how they harnessed the natural hot springs nearly 2,000 years ago. Sample the mineral-rich spa water and learn about Bath's transformation from Roman settlement to fashionable Georgian spa town.\n\nStroll through Bath's picturesque streets lined with honey-colored limestone buildings, including the famous Royal Crescent and Circus. The city's compact center makes it perfect for exploring on foot, with plenty of opportunities to admire Jane Austen's former home city and its architectural masterpieces.\n\nThis expertly guided tour provides fascinating historical commentary, comfortable transportation, and carefully timed visits to avoid crowds. Perfect for history enthusiasts, culture lovers, and anyone seeking to experience England's ancient past in a single memorable day.	["Explore the mysterious 5,000-year-old Stonehenge stone circle", "Discover the remarkably preserved Roman Baths and Sacred Spring", "Walk through Bath's stunning Georgian architecture and Royal Crescent", "Learn fascinating theories about Stonehenge's purpose and construction", "Sample natural spa water from the ancient Roman springs", "Enjoy expert commentary on British history and heritage", "Visit two UNESCO World Heritage Sites in one day", "Travel through beautiful English countryside"]	["Round-trip transportation from London", "Professional English-speaking guide", "Entrance tickets to Stonehenge", "Entrance tickets to Roman Baths", "Audio guide at Stonehenge", "Free time to explore Bath city center"]	["Food and drinks", "Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Gratuities", "Personal expenses", "Additional attractions in Bath"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for personal expenses	This tour involves considerable walking on uneven surfaces. Weather can change quickly, so dress in layers. The tour operates in all weather conditions.	89.00	62.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	660	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Victoria Coach Station	Meet at Victoria Coach Station, Gate 1-5. Please arrive 15 minutes before departure time.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Moderate	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739420/rayna/activities/8e443588-b27b-4e80-b27e