e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb	London: Tower of London and Crown Jewels Exhibition Ticket	london-tower-of-london-and-crown-jewels-exhibition-ticket-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Historical Site	Self-guided	null	draft	Visit the historic Tower of London, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and marvel at the Crown Jewels collection with 23,578 gems including the Imperial State Crown.	Take a tour of the timeless Tower of London – part of British history since the 11th century. This UNESCO World Heritage Site was built in 1086 by William the Conqueror. Discover London's castle – a secure fortress, royal palace, and infamous prison. Spot the ravens that live on the premises and find out why they are known as the guardians of the Tower. Stroll across Tower Green to see where many executions took place, including those of 2 of Henry VIII's wives. You will also have access to the inside of the tower. Prepare to be dazzled by the Crown Jewels of the United Kingdom. These priceless symbols of the British Monarchy compose the greatest working collection of crown jewels in the world. Marvel over the 23,578 gems, including the glistening Imperial State Crown - this piece alone has 2,868 diamonds, 273 pearls, 17 sapphires, 11 emeralds, and 5 rubies. Gain valuable insights into the Tower of London's history from some of its most famous residents, the Yeoman Body. The Yeoman Warders will be on hand to provide fascinating stories of the Tower through the ages.	["Visit the UNESCO World Heritage Site Tower of London", "Marvel at the Crown Jewels with 23,578 gems", "See the Imperial State Crown with 2,868 diamonds", "Learn about the Tower's history as fortress, palace, and prison", "Spot the ravens known as guardians of the Tower", "Visit Tower Green where executions took place", "Meet Yeoman Warders for fascinating historical stories"]	["Access to Tower of London", "Crown Jewels Exhibition", "Yeoman Warder stories and insights"]	["Food and beverages", "Transportation to/from Tower of London", "Private guided tours", "Souvenir photos", "Parking fees"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera (photography allowed in most areas except Crown Jewels), and valid ID for security checks	Security screening is required for entry. Photography is not permitted in the Crown Jewels exhibition. The Tower can be very busy during peak times, especially weekends and school holidays. Some areas may have restricted access during special events or ceremonies.	33.60	16.80	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["09:00", "09:30", "10:00", "10:30", "11:00", "11:30", "12:00", "12:30", "13:00", "13:30", "14:00", "14:30", "15:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the visit date for a full refund	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Tower of London	Enter through the main visitor entrance on the south side of the Tower of London, near Tower Bridge. The entrance is clearly marked with signs and ticket validation points.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739463/rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739463/rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Tower of London and Crown Jewels Exhibition Ticket - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739465/rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb/1.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Tower of London and Crown Jewels Exhibition Ticket - image 2", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-b7a7-93755d9f56eb/1"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739466/rayna/activities/e68e5a69-69a2-4a5b-