f15002ea-5bb1-48e9-91d4-8befdc959c6a	From London: Stonehenge Morning Day Trip with Admission	from-london-stonehenge-morning-day-trip-with-admission-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Historical Site Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Experience the mysterious stone circle of Stonehenge on this morning tour from London. Discover this ancient World Heritage Site with spectacular countryside views.	Visit one of the most famous pre-historic sites in the world on this half-day morning tour to Stonehenge. Your priority group admission ticket is included, allowing access to the monument, exhibition and site shuttle bus. Depart London at 7:30 AM to be some of the first visitors that arrive at the site. Learn about the history of this monument from your driver/guide, and take advantage of the audio-guides available upon arrival. Situated on Salisbury Plain in the Wiltshire countryside, Stonehenge is said to have been constructed more than 5,000 years ago. Enjoy the views of the surrounding plain, visit the monument, and explore the exhibition for approximately 2 hours. Head back to Central London for around 2 PM, so you'll have time to explore London for the rest of the day.	["Marvel at the world-famous Stonehenge Stone Circle with a skip-the-line ticket", "Explore Britain's most important prehistoric monument and exhibition", "Take in panoramic views of the English countryside", "Be among the first visitors to arrive at the site", "Learn about 5,000+ years of history from your driver/guide"]	["Admission to Stonehenge Monument & Exhibition", "Downloadable Audio-guide at Stonehenge", "Air-conditioned transportation", "Driver/guide"]	["Food and drinks", "Hotel pickup and drop-off"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and water bottle. Dress in layers as weather can change quickly on Salisbury Plain.	Tour operates in all weather conditions. The monument is located outdoors with limited shelter. Early departure time of 7:30 AM requires punc