f6befa14-d8e7-4b15-bcf9-e9d46746eb1d	From London: Canterbury & White Cliffs of Dover Tour	from-london-canterbury-white-cliffs-of-dover-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Nature & History	Group tour	null	draft	Small group day tour from London exploring Canterbury Cathedral city and the dramatic White Cliffs of Dover coastline.	Embark on an unforgettable day trip from London to explore two of England's most iconic destinations: the historic cathedral city of Canterbury and the breathtaking White Cliffs of Dover. This carefully crafted small group tour combines rich medieval history with stunning natural beauty, offering you the perfect escape from the bustling capital.\n\nYour journey begins with a scenic drive through the picturesque Kent countryside, known as the 'Garden of England' for its rolling hills and charming villages. Upon arriving in Canterbury, you'll step into a living piece of history. The magnificent Canterbury Cathedral, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and mother church of the Anglican Communion, has been a pilgrimage destination for over 800 years. Marvel at its soaring Gothic architecture, intricate stained glass windows, and the shrine of Thomas Becket, the archbishop martyred here in 1170.\n\nWander through Canterbury's cobbled streets, where medieval timber-framed buildings house boutique shops, traditional pubs, and cozy cafés. The city's Roman walls and ruins tell stories spanning two millennia, while the charming River Stour adds to the town's romantic atmosphere.\n\nNext, journey to the dramatic White Cliffs of Dover, one of Britain's most recognizable natural landmarks. These iconic chalk cliffs rise majestically from the English Channel, offering spectacular panoramic views across to France on clear days. The cliffs have served as a symbol of hope and homecoming for countless travelers and hold deep significance in British history and culture.\n\nExplore the cliff-top paths where wildflowers bloom in spring and summer, and breathe in the fresh sea air while watching ships navigate the world's busiest shipping lane. The visitor center provides fascinating insights into the area's geology, wildlife, and wartime history, including the secret tunnels used during World War II.\n\nThis expertly guided tour ensures you experience the best of both destinations while learning about their fascinating histories, making it an ideal day out for history enthusiasts, nature lovers, and anyone seeking to discover England's heritage beyond London.	["Small group"]	["Professional English-speaking guide", "Comfortable air-conditioned coach transport", "Canterbury Cathedral entrance fee", "White Cliffs of Dover visitor center access", "Small group experience (maximum 16 passengers)", "Commentary on English history and culture"]	["Food and drinks", "Gratuities (optional)", "Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Personal expenses", "Travel insurance"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for personal expenses. Bring layers as coastal weather can change quickly.	This tour involves moderate walking on uneven surfaces including cobblestones and cliff paths. Canterbury Cathedral may have restricted access during special services. Weather conditions may affect visibility at the White Cliffs.	89.00	62.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	570	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour start time. No refund for cancellations made less than 24 hours in advance.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Victoria Coach Station	Meet at Victoria Coach Station, Gate 1-5 area. The exact gate will be confirmed in your booking confirmation. Arrive 15 minutes before departure time.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Moderate	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739617/rayna/activities/f6befa14-d8e7-4b15-bcf9-e9d46746eb1d/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://re