abde93f0-abe1-4018-90f2-45327603b28f	From London: 7 Unmissable Cotswolds Stops Small-Group Tour	from-london-7-unmissable-cotswolds-stops-small-group-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Countryside Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Small group day tour from London visiting seven picturesque villages and towns in the beautiful Cotswolds countryside.	Escape the bustling streets of London and immerse yourself in the quintessential English countryside with this comprehensive small-group tour of the Cotswolds. This full-day adventure takes you through seven carefully selected villages and towns that showcase the very best of this Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty. Travel in comfort with a maximum of 16 passengers, ensuring a personalized experience as you explore honey-colored stone cottages, rolling green hills, and charming market towns that have remained virtually unchanged for centuries.\n\nYour journey begins with a scenic drive through the picturesque Cotswolds landscape, where you'll visit iconic destinations including the medieval wool town of Chipping Campden, the romantic village of Bourton-on-the-Water known as the 'Venice of the Cotswolds,' and the historic market town of Stow-on-the-Wold. Each stop offers unique photo opportunities and time to explore at your own pace, from browsing local shops selling traditional crafts to enjoying a traditional pub lunch in an authentic English setting.\n\nThe tour also includes visits to lesser-known gems like the enchanting village of Upper and Lower Slaughter, consistently voted among England's most beautiful villages. Your knowledgeable guide will share fascinating stories about the region's rich history, from its medieval wool trade heritage to its connections with famous writers and artists. You'll learn about traditional Cotswolds architecture, local customs, and the area's significance in English culture.\n\nThis carefully crafted itinerary balances guided commentary with free time for personal exploration, allowing you to soak in the peaceful atmosphere of rural England. Whether you're interested in history, photography, or simply seeking a tranquil escape from city life, this tour offers an authentic taste of the English countryside that has captivated visitors for generations.	["Visit seven picturesque Cotswolds villages including Bourton-on-the-Water and Chipping Campden", "Small group experience with maximum 16 passengers for personalized attention", "Explore the 'Venice of the Cotswolds' and England's most beautiful villages", "Discover honey-colored stone cottages and medieval market towns", "Learn about the region's rich wool trade history and cultural heritage", "Enjoy free time for shopping, photography, and exploring at your own pace", "Experience authentic English countryside atmosphere away from London crowds", "Professional guide sharing local stories and historical insights"]	["Round-trip transportation from London in comfortable vehicle", "Professional English-speaking guide", "Small group tour (maximum 16 passengers)", "Visits to seven Cotswolds villages and towns", "Free time for exploration and photography"]	["Food and drinks", "Entrance fees to attractions", "Personal expenses and souvenirs", "Gratuities for guide", "Hotel pickup and drop-off"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for lunch and souvenirs	This tour involves moderate walking on uneven surfaces in historic villages. Weather can be unpredictable, so dress in layers. Some villages may have limited facilities.	89.00	62.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	600	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Central London meeting point	Specific meeting point details provided upon booking confirmation	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0