c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c	London: Tower Bridge Entry Ticket	london-tower-bridge-entry-ticket-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Historical Attraction	Self-guided	null	draft	Visit Tower Bridge, one of London's most famous landmarks, and experience Victorian history with stunning glass walkway views 42 metres above the Thames.	A trip to London wouldn't be complete without a visit to Tower Bridge, one of the city's most famous landmarks. A visit to Tower Bridge will take you back to the Victorian era, immersing you in the landmarks story from the very beginning. Marvel at the views of the city from the stunning glass walkway, set 42 metres above the River Thames. Situated between the North and South Towers, you can enjoy awe inspiring and unique views of the city. You can also read all about the history and construction of Tower Bridge. Take a trip back in time and discover the impressive Victorian Engine Rooms that once powered Tower Bridge. See where more than 80 people were needed to operate the engines and raise the bridge. The engine rooms will ignite your senses to get a feel of what it was like back in the Victorian era. See the former workers of Tower Bridge forever immortalised in the Blue Line that leads from the Towers to the historic Engine Rooms. The Blue Line shines light on some of the unsung heroes who kept the famous landmark in motion.	["Marvel at views from the glass walkway 42 metres above the River Thames", "Discover the impressive Victorian Engine Rooms that once powered Tower Bridge", "Learn about the history and construction of Tower Bridge", "See the Blue Line showcasing the unsung heroes who kept the landmark in motion", "Experience what it was like in the Victorian era", "Enjoy unique views of London from between the North and South Towers"]	["Entry ticket to Tower Bridge Exhibition", "Access to high-level walkways with glass floors", "Access to Victorian Engine Rooms", "Interactive displays and exhibitions", "Self-guided tour materials", "Blue Line trail experience"]	["Audio guide (available for additional fee)", "Food and beverages", "Transportation to/from Tower Bridge", "Guided tour service", "Souvenir photographs"]	Comfortable walking shoes, camera for photos, and weather-appropriate clothing as some areas may be cooler	The glass floor walkways may not be suitable for visitors with severe vertigo or fear of heights. The venue is wheelchair accessible with lifts to all levels. Last entry is typically 30 minutes before closing time.	12.30	6.20	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["10:00", "10:30", "11:00", "11:30", "12:00", "12:30", "13:00", "13:30", "14:00", "14:30", "15:00", "15:30", "16:00", "16:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the experience starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Tower Bridge	Enter via the North Tower entrance on Tower Bridge Road, next to the Tower Bridge Gift Shop	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739701/rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739701/rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Tower Bridge Entry Ticket - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739703/rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/1.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Tower Bridge Entry Ticket - image 2", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/1"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739705/rayna/activities/c3a339b6-dbd2-49a6-8411-0cc25ea8d15c/2.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Tower Bridge Entry Ticket - image 3", "size_variant": "detail", "c