33927601-f856-424f-8593-2def822b3b29	London: St Paul's Cathedral Entry Ticket	london-st-paul-s-cathedral-entry-ticket-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Cathedral Tour	Self-guided	null	draft	Explore St. Paul's Cathedral, an architectural masterpiece and England's place of national celebration with multimedia guides included.	Today St Paul's is both a busy working Anglican Cathedral and one of London's leading sightseeing attractions. Touchscreen multimedia guides are now included for sightseers; listen and watch, as the guide uses film, new photography, and detailed commentary to offer an effective interpretation of this unique landmark. Opt for a more personal approach with tours of the cathedral floor and crypt led by cathedral guides 4 times daily; join in at no extra cost as you spend 60 minutes walking through the cathedral and learning about its art, its history, and its religious significance. Alternatively, join one of various short introductory talks offered throughout the day for a snippet of additional insight. These guided tours and talks are available on a first come first served basis. As you walk through the cathedral, you will notice it is filled with natural light, glittering mosaics, and paintings adorning its dome interior. See the chapels on the ground floor, then, for those who are able, climb the 257 steps to the Whispering Gallery to test the unique acoustics. Climb 119 further steps to the Stone Gallery and then 152 final steps to the Golden Gallery, both of which afford spectacular panoramic views of the city. Take time to visit the crypt to view the many tombs and memorials to world-famous Britons, including Lord Admiral Nelson and the Duke of Wellington.	["Explore St. Paul's Cathedral with included multimedia guides", "Join free guided tours of the cathedral floor and crypt 4 times daily", "Climb 257 steps to the Whispering Gallery to test unique acoustics", "Visit Stone Gallery and Golden Gallery for panoramic city views", "See natural light, glittering mosaics, and dome interior paintings", "Visit the crypt with tombs of Lord Admiral Nelson and Duke of Wellington", "Experience both working Anglican Cathedral and leading sightseeing attraction"]	["Entry ticket to St Paul's Cathedral", "Touchscreen multimedia guides", "Access to guided tours and talks (first come first served)"]	["Audio guide in languages other than English", "Photography inside the cathedral", "Food and beverages", "Transportation to/from the cathedral", "Gratuities"]	Comfortable walking shoes for climbing steps, camera for exterior photos only, water bottle for hydration during climb	Photography and filming are not permitted inside the cathedral. The climb to the galleries involves 528 steps and may not be suitable for those with mobility issues or heart conditions. Last admission is typically 30 minutes before closing time.	25.00	11.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["08:30", "09:00", "09:30", "10:00", "10:30", "11:00", "11:30", "12:00", "12:30", "13:00", "13:30", "14:00", "14:30", "15:00", "15:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the experience starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	St Paul's Cathedral	Main entrance of St. Paul's Cathedral on St. Paul's Churchyard	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Moderate	Intermediate	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739790/rayna/activities/33927601-f856-424f-8593-2def822b3b29/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739790/rayna/activities/33927601-f856-424f-8593-2def822b3b29/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: St Paul's Cathedral Entry Ticket - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/33927601-f856-424f-8593-2def822b3b29/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775739792/rayna/activities/33927601-f856-424f-8593-2def822b3b29/1.jpg", "alt_text": "London: St Paul's C