5d910645-b1a7-4964-ab09-4733e29cf823	Buckingham Palace, Westminster Abbey & Big Ben Tour	buckingham-palace-westminster-abbey-big-ben-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Walking Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Guided tour of London's royal and political landmarks including Buckingham Palace, Westminster Abbey, and Big Ben.	Embark on an unforgettable journey through London's most iconic royal and political landmarks on this comprehensive 5-hour walking tour. Discover the rich history and grandeur of Britain's monarchy and government as you explore three of the capital's most significant sites: Buckingham Palace, Westminster Abbey, and Big Ben.\n\nBegin your adventure at the magnificent Buckingham Palace, the official residence of the British Royal Family. Marvel at the stunning architecture and learn fascinating stories about royal traditions, ceremonies, and the daily life of the monarchy. Your expert guide will share insider knowledge about the palace's 775 rooms and its role in British history.\n\nNext, step inside the breathtaking Westminster Abbey, a UNESCO World Heritage Site that has witnessed over 1,000 years of British history. This Gothic masterpiece has hosted 39 coronations, including Queen Elizabeth II's in 1953, and serves as the final resting place for monarchs, poets, and notable figures like Charles Darwin and Stephen Hawking. Admire the stunning architecture, intricate stone carvings, and beautiful stained glass windows while learning about the abbey's pivotal role in British culture.\n\nConclude your tour at the iconic Big Ben and the Houses of Parliament, symbols of British democracy and governance. Though currently under restoration, Big Ben remains one of London's most photographed landmarks. Your guide will explain the fascinating history of this Victorian masterpiece and the political significance of the Palace of Westminster.\n\nThis immersive experience combines historical insights, architectural appreciation, and cultural understanding, making it perfect for first-time visitors and history enthusiasts alike. With skip-the-line access and expert commentary, you'll gain deep insights into the traditions, ceremonies, and stories that have shaped modern Britain.	["Explore the official residence of the British Royal Family at Buckingham Palace", "Step inside Westminster Abbey, coronation site of British monarchs for nearly 1,000 years", "Discover the Gothic architecture and royal tombs within Westminster Abbey", "Learn about British political history at the Houses of Parliament and Big Ben", "Enjoy expert commentary from knowledgeable local guides", "Skip-the-line access to Westminster Abbey", "Walk through London's historic Westminster district", "See the Poets' Corner and Coronation Chair inside the Abbey"]	["Professional English-speaking guide", "Skip-the-line entrance to Westminster Abbey", "5-hour guided walking tour", "Historical commentary and insights", "Small group experience"]	["Interior access to Buckingham Palace (exterior viewing only)", "Food and beverages", "Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Gratuities", "Personal expenses"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and water bottle. Note that large bags are not permitted inside Westminster Abbey.	Westminster Abbey has a strict dress code - no shorts, sleeveless tops, or flip-flops. Photography is not permitted inside the Abbey. The tour involves considerable walking and standing. Big Ben is currently under restoration until 2024.	65.00	45.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	300	["09:00", "14:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts. No refund for cancellations made less than 24 hours in advance.	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Westminster Underground Station	Meet outside Westminster Underground Station, Exit 1 (Big Ben exit). Look for the guide holding a sign with the tour company nam