324e233a-3e91-4d78-8830-ec664ce2a91c	From London: Cotswolds and Oxford Guided Day-Trip	from-london-cotswolds-and-oxford-guided-day-trip-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Countryside Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Guided day trip from London exploring the picturesque Cotswolds countryside and the historic university city of Oxford.	Escape the bustling streets of London and immerse yourself in the quintessential English countryside on this captivating full-day guided tour to the Cotswolds and Oxford. This carefully crafted journey takes you through some of England's most picturesque landscapes, combining the honey-colored stone villages of the Cotswolds with the prestigious academic atmosphere of Oxford University.\n\nYour adventure begins with a scenic drive through the rolling hills of the Cotswolds, an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty renowned for its timeless charm and architectural heritage. Marvel at the distinctive limestone buildings that seem to glow golden in the sunlight, and explore charming market towns where time appears to have stood still. Visit traditional villages like Bourton-on-the-Water, often called the 'Venice of the Cotswolds' for its low bridges spanning the River Windrush, or the medieval wool town of Chipping Campden with its historic market hall.\n\nThe journey continues to Oxford, the 'City of Dreaming Spires,' where centuries of academic excellence have shaped one of the world's most prestigious universities. Walk through the ancient cobblestone streets and discover the magnificent college buildings that have educated kings, prime ministers, and Nobel Prize winners. Your knowledgeable guide will share fascinating stories about famous alumni, architectural marvels, and the traditions that make Oxford unique.\n\nExplore iconic locations such as the Bodleian Library, one of Europe's oldest libraries, and admire the stunning architecture of colleges like Christ Church, which inspired scenes in the Harry Potter films. The tour provides ample opportunities for photography, shopping for local crafts, and experiencing authentic English pub culture.\n\nThis comprehensive day trip offers the perfect blend of natural beauty, historical significance, and cultural immersion, making it an ideal way to experience the very best of rural England and academic tradition in a single memorable day.	["Explore the honey-colored stone villages of the picturesque Cotswolds countryside", "Visit the prestigious Oxford University and its historic colleges", "Walk through charming market towns like Bourton-on-the-Water", "Discover the famous Bodleian Library and Christ Church College", "Enjoy scenic drives through Areas of Outstanding Natural Beauty", "Learn about English history and traditions from expert local guides", "Experience authentic English village atmosphere and architecture", "See filming locations from popular movies and TV shows"]	["Round-trip transportation from London in comfortable coach", "Professional English-speaking guide", "Guided walking tours of Cotswolds villages", "Guided tour of Oxford University and colleges", "Free time for shopping and exploration", "Commentary on history, culture, and local traditions"]	["Food and beverages", "Entrance fees to specific college buildings (if applicable)", "Personal expenses and souvenirs", "Gratuities for guide and driver", "Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Travel insurance"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for personal expenses and optional entrance fees.	This tour involves moderate walking on cobblestone streets and uneven surfaces. Weather can be unpredictable, so layered clothing is recommended. Some college buildings may have restricted access during exam periods or special events.	65.00	45.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	630	["08:30", "09:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour start time for a full