0862d047-4b0d-4c3b-be1c-21e93a6517ad	From London: Small-Group Full-Day Cotswolds Guided Tour	from-london-small-group-full-day-cotswolds-guided-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Countryside Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Small group full-day guided tour from London exploring the charming villages and countryside of the Cotswolds.	Escape the bustling streets of London and immerse yourself in the quintessential English countryside with this small-group full-day guided tour of the Cotswolds. This carefully curated journey takes you through one of England's most picturesque regions, designated as an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty. Your expert guide will lead you through honey-colored stone villages, rolling hills, and charming market towns that have remained virtually unchanged for centuries.\n\nThe tour typically includes visits to iconic Cotswolds villages such as Bourton-on-the-Water, often called the 'Venice of the Cotswolds' for its low bridges spanning the River Windrush, and Stow-on-the-Wold, a historic market town with its famous market square surrounded by antique shops and cozy pubs. You'll also explore the medieval wool town of Chipping Campden, renowned for its magnificent 15th-century church and perfectly preserved high street.\n\nThroughout the day, you'll discover the rich history of the region, from its medieval wool trade heritage to its connection with the Arts and Crafts movement. Your knowledgeable guide will share fascinating stories about local traditions, architecture, and the famous residents who have called the Cotswolds home. The small group size ensures a personalized experience with plenty of opportunities to ask questions and capture stunning photographs.\n\nThe tour includes comfortable transportation in a modern vehicle, allowing you to relax and enjoy the scenic countryside views between villages. You'll have free time to explore each location independently, browse local shops for unique souvenirs, and perhaps enjoy a traditional English pub lunch (at your own expense). This immersive experience offers the perfect blend of guided commentary and independent exploration, making it ideal for first-time visitors and photography enthusiasts alike.	["Small group"]	["Professional English-speaking guide", "Transportation in comfortable air-conditioned vehicle", "Small group tour (maximum 16 passengers)", "Entrance to villages and walking tours", "Commentary on history and local culture"]	["Food and drinks", "Entrance fees to paid attractions", "Personal expenses and souvenirs", "Gratuities for guide", "Hotel pickup and drop-off"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for lunch and personal expenses	Tour operates in all weather conditions. Villages involve walking on uneven surfaces and cobblestones. Lunch stop is included but meals are at your own expense.	65.00	45.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	600	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Victoria Coach Station	Meet at Victoria Coach Station, Gate 1-5 area. Please arrive 15 minutes before departure time.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Easy	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740119/rayna/activities/0862d047-4b0d-4c3b-be1c-21e93a6517ad/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740119/rayna/activities/0862d047-4b0d-4c3b-be1c-21e93a6517ad/0.jpg", "alt_text": "From London: Small-Group Full-Day Cotswolds Guided Tour - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/0862d047-4b0d-4c3b-be1c-21e93a6517ad/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740122/rayna/activities/0862d047-4b0d-4c3b-be1c-21e93a6517ad/1.jpg", "alt_text": "From London: Small-Group Full-Day Cotswolds Guided Tour - image 2", "size_variant": "detail", "c