be4c41ef-8239-43de-8465-2f55c8a61edd	London: Wembley Stadium Guided Tour	london-wembley-stadium-guided-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Stadium Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Follow in the footsteps of legends on a guided tour of Wembley Stadium, exploring behind the scenes of the UK's largest sports and music venue.	Follow in the footsteps of legends on the Wembley Stadium Tour. Explore behind the scenes of the UK's largest sports and music venue, which has played host to some of the greatest footballers and performers throughout its long and storied history. Meet your guide beside the statue of Bobby Moore, England's captain during 1966 their World Cup win. Go deep into the heart of the stadium and visit the dressing rooms, the press conference room, the players' tunnel, pitchside, and climb the famous steps to where trophies are presented. Relive the stadium's greatest moments such as England's 1966 World Cup victory, various UEFA Champions League triumphs, the beloved annual tradition of the Emirates FA Cup Final, and countless sell-out concerts. Be astounded by the design and scale of this 90,000-seater venue. Discover the Crossbar Exhibition and The Walk of Legends which highlight the stadium's origins, rich history, and heritage dating back as far as The British Empire Exhibition of 1924.	["Visit the dressing rooms and press conference room", "Walk through the players' tunnel to pitchside", "Climb the famous steps where trophies are presented", "Explore the Crossbar Exhibition", "Experience The Walk of Legends", "Learn about the stadium's history from 1924 to present", "See the iconic 440-meter-high arch", "Discover the venue that hosts 90,000 spectators"]	["Professional guided tour of Wembley Stadium", "Access to team dressing rooms and players' tunnel", "Visit to the Royal Box and trophy presentation area", "Entry to The Walk of Legends exhibition", "Access to Crossbar Exhibition", "Pitchside access for photos", "Expert commentary on st