db4d3d10-fa18-430c-abcd-37cb2e04f8e5	London's most comprehensive and exclusive Harry Potter tour	london-s-most-comprehensive-and-exclusive-harry-potter-tour-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Cultural	Movie Tour	Group tour	null	draft	Visit 18 Harry Potter filming locations across London including King's Cross, Leadenhall Market, and Borough Market with a Ravenclaw House prefect guide.	We will start our tour at the most famous train station in the wizarding world: King's Cross Station. There, Rubén, your Ravenclaw House prefect (holding a dark blue umbrella), will be waiting for you to begin our adventure. We will see 18 scenes from the 8 films in the series, including Leadenhall Market, famous for being Diagon Alley in Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone; Borough Market, known for being the Leaky Cauldron in Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban; the Millennium Footbridge, which is destroyed in Harry Potter and the Half-Blood Prince; and Scotland Yard, which appears as the Ministry of Magic in Harry Potter and the Order of the Phoenix and Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 1. We will also visit the official Harry Potter shop at King's Cross and an alleyway that served as inspiration for the books. On this tour, we will also see locations from various films, such as Bridget Jones's Diary, Mission: Impossible, and Mary Poppins Returns, and of course, some scenes from the new HBO Harry Potter series. We will end at Godwin's Court, very close to Leicester Square. This tour has been designed to visit as many Harry Potter locations in London as possible in the shortest possible time. Therefore, the walking route covers 3.7 miles (6 km), with two tube rides, and takes you through parts of the City of London and the City of Westminster.	["Visit 18 Harry Potter filming locations from all 8 films", "See Leadenhall Market (Diagon Alley)", "Explore Borough Market (The Leaky Cauldron)", "Walk across the Millennium Footbridge", "Visit Scotland Yard (Ministry of Magic)", "Stop at the official Harry Potter shop at King's Cross", "Small groups of maximum 15 people", "Covers 3.7 miles with two tube rides"]	["Guided tour with Ravenclaw House prefect", "Visit to 18 Harry Potter filming locations", "Two tube rides", "Visit to official Harry Potter shop"]	["Transportation costs (2 tube rides required)", "Food and beverages", "Entrance fees to attractions", "Purchases at Harry Potter shop", "Gratuities"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera or smartphone for photos, Oyster card or contactless payment for tube travel, and enthusiasm for the wizarding world	This tour involves 3.7 miles of walking and includes two tube rides. The tour operates in all weather conditions, so please dress appropriately. Meeting point is at King's Cross Station - look for your guide with a dark blue umbrella. The tour covers locations in both the City of London and Westminster.	25.00	18.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	0	["10:00", "14:00"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour start time	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	King's Cross Station	Rubén, your Ravenclaw House prefect (holding a dark blue umbrella), will be waiting for you	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Moderate	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740625/rayna/activities/db4d3d10-fa18-430c-abcd-37cb2e04f8e5/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740625/rayna/activities/db4d3d10-fa18-430c-abcd-37cb2e04f8e5/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London's most comprehensive and exclusive Harry Potter tour - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id": "rayna/activities/db4d3d10-fa18-430c-abcd-37cb2e04f8e5/0"}, {"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775740626/rayna/activities/db4d3d10-fa18-430c-abcd-37cb2e04f8e5/1.jpg", "alt_text": "London's most comprehensive and excl