563a3400-ea4f-4992-a2a1-278ccf5ade77	London: Windsor, Stonehenge, Bath, and Roman Baths Day Trip	london-windsor-stonehenge-bath-and-roman-baths-day-trip-london	c5cda0a7-0b95-4a26-a8b4-1001b81014a5	Day Trip	Historical Sites	Group tour	null	draft	Comprehensive day trip from London visiting Windsor Castle, Stonehenge, Bath city, and the famous Roman Baths.	Embark on an unforgettable full-day journey from London to explore three of England's most iconic historical destinations. This comprehensive day trip takes you through centuries of British history, from royal residences to ancient mysteries and Roman heritage. Begin your adventure at Windsor Castle, the world's oldest occupied castle and official residence of the British Royal Family. Explore the magnificent State Apartments, St. George's Chapel, and Queen Mary's Dolls' House while learning about over 900 years of royal history. Continue to the mystical Stonehenge, one of the world's most famous prehistoric monuments. Stand in awe of these ancient stone circles that have puzzled archaeologists and visitors for millennia, dating back over 5,000 years. The audio guide reveals fascinating theories about this UNESCO World Heritage Site's purpose and construction. Your final destination is the beautiful Georgian city of Bath, renowned for its stunning architecture and natural hot springs. Discover the remarkably preserved Roman Baths, where you can walk on ancient pavements and see the Sacred Spring, Roman Temple, and the Great Bath. The interactive audio guide brings the Roman experience to life as you explore these 2,000-year-old thermal springs. Stroll through Bath's elegant streets, admiring the honey-colored limestone buildings and perhaps visiting the famous Pump Room. This expertly guided tour combines comfortable transportation with fascinating commentary, making it the perfect way to experience England's rich heritage in a single day. With skip-the-line access and expert local insights, you'll maximize your time at each incredible location.	["Explore Windsor Castle, the world's oldest occupied castle and royal residence", "Marvel at the mysterious 5,000-year-old stone circles of Stonehenge", "Discover the ancient Roman Baths and taste the mineral-rich spa water", "Walk through Bath's stunning Georgian architecture and UNESCO World Heritage streets", "Enjoy comfortable transportation and expert commentary throughout the day", "Skip-the-line access to all major attractions", "Visit three UNESCO World Heritage Sites in one incredible day", "Learn about over 2,000 years of British history from Romans to Royalty"]	["Round-trip transportation from central London", "Professional tour guide", "Entry to Windsor Castle", "Entry to Stonehenge with audio guide", "Entry to Roman Baths with audio guide", "Free time to explore Bath city center"]	["Food and drinks", "Gratuities", "Hotel pickup and drop-off", "Personal expenses"]	Comfortable walking shoes, weather-appropriate clothing, camera, and some cash for personal purchases	This tour involves considerable walking and standing. Windsor Castle may have restricted areas during royal events. Weather can change quickly, so dress in layers.	89.00	79.00	\N	\N	\N	GBP	Per person	\N	0.00	690	["08:30"]	["Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday", "Sunday"]	f	f	24	Free cancellation up to 24 hours before the tour starts	\N	\N	\N	United Kingdom	London	\N	London	0.000000	0.000000	\N	Victoria Coach Station	Meet at Victoria Coach Station, Gate 1-5 area. Please arrive 15 minutes before departure time.	\N	f	\N	f	f	\N	\N	\N	Moderate	Beginner	f	\N	["en"]	https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738950/rayna/activities/563a3400-ea4f-4992-a2a1-278ccf5ade77/0.jpg	[{"url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/dykbg0noa/image/upload/v1775738950/rayna/activities/563a3400-ea4f-4992-a2a1-278ccf5ade77/0.jpg", "alt_text": "London: Windsor, Stonehenge, Bath, and Roman Baths Day Trip - image 1", "size_variant": "detail", "cloudinary_id":