a8ccbde1-746c-43f2-8f1d-3cb052e1e14d	70ce258c-53f6-47cb-ac2f-b4c6c4744276	Anonymous	\N	3.00	Disappointing New Year's Eve Celestial Cruise – Not as Advertised	We booked the New Year's Eve on the Celestial Cruise through Golden Tours for our family (including our 12-year-old son), excited for his dream of seeing the London fireworks from a boat on the Thames. The voucher and promotions promised a deluxe individual basket (with champagne/Prosecco, bagels, and snacks), live music, smart casual dress code (no jeans/trainers), comfortable seating, boarding from 9:00 PM, and return around 1:00 AM. Unfortunately, none of that matched the reality: No deluxe baskets or meals were provided (staff were confused when asked and dismissed it). No soft drinks for our child. We waited over an hour in the cold outside (arrived on time but boarding delayed until nearly 10:00 PM). Dress code ignored (lots of jeans/trainers), no proper seating/tables available, and some inappropriate staff behavior/music by the end. Returned late (~1:30 AM). It ruined what should have been a special family night. Golden Tours apologised for the missing basket and other issues, and after several emails, they agreed to a 50% refund—which we've accepted to close the matter. However, the experience was far from what was sold, and the whole process was frustrating. I hope sharing this helps other families avoid similar disappointment or get fair resolution if things go wrong.	December 31, 2025	trustpilot	https://www.trustpilot.com/review/www.goldentours.com?page=4	f	en	2026-04-10 12:37:09.258836+05:30
